`LZ4F_makeBlock` advances `((U32)crcFlag)*BFSize` = 8 bytes (`:789` vs `:903-907`).\n3. **`LZ4F_compressUpdateImpl:1013-1017` lacks `FORWARD_IF_ERROR`** on its internal `LZ4F_flush` — an error code is added to `dstPtr` as if it were a byte count.\n4. **`LZ4F_writeClose` swallows earlier write failures** (`lz4file.c:325-340`): if `errCode` was latched, `compressEnd` is skipped and `LZ4F_OK_NoError` is returned, leaving an unterminated frame.\n5. **Two genuinely dead error sites**: `lz4file.c:162` (`io_read`, unreachable — `size_t` can't be negative) and `lz4file.c:124` (`maxBlockSize_invalid` on a decoded 3-bit field already validated by `decodeHeader`).\n6. **`LZ4_setStreamDecode` can never return 0** despite its documented `0 == error` contract (`lz4.c:2589-2602`).\n7. **`XXH32_reset`/`XXH64_reset` do not NULL-check `statePtr`** — they `memcpy` into it. The task brief anticipated `XXH_ERROR` here; the actual code has no such check, so a Rust port must not model this as a recoverable error.\n8. **`*_continue` decoders conflate empty output with failure** (`result <= 0` → early return, state un-advanced) at `lz4.c:2640/2653/2662/2685/2694/2703`.\n\nThe closing note lists the unreachable `LZ4F_ERROR_*` codes with reasons: `GENERIC`, `blockMode_invalid`, `compressionLevel_invalid`, `srcSize_tooLarge` (never emitted at all), `allocation_failed` (environmental only), `maxCode` (sentinel), plus the conditionally-compiled-out checksum/magic errors under `FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4833,"cache_read_input_tokens":186792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4833,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017hqUQKXJpd7ufkH9BeT6Dv","session_id":"fbbc4e99-c89f-4b88-83bb-165c018df800","uuid":"65a545b8-964a-4895-9c28-4fafe2e5f785","timestamp":"2026