{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a45f5ec5292f133b7","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017hqUQKXJpd7ufkH9BeT6Dv","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-5nSRwn/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-gKqcQz/fbbc4e99-c89f-4b88-83bb-165c018df800/tasks/a45f5ec5292f133b7.output","summary":"Done. `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-gKqcQz/translation/ERRORS.md` is written: **311 lines, 236 table rows**, every row traced to a `file:line` in `c_src/src/`.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- **lz4frame.c** (rows 1–80): every `RETURN_ERROR` / `RETURN_ERROR_IF` site with its exact `LZ4F_ERROR_*` code, plus every `FORWARD_IF_ERROR` propagation point.\n- **lz4file.c** (rows 81–105): all 17 error sites across `readOpen/read/readClose/writeOpen/write/writeClose`.\n- **lz4.c** (rows 106–178): `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` rejections, all three `limitedOutput` `return 0` sites, all `_output_error` gotos in both the fast and safe decode loops, `read_variable_length`'s three `rvl_error` returns, `LZ4_initStream`'s three `NULL` returns, `loadDict`/`saveDict`/`decoderRingBufferSize`/`setStreamDecode` edge behaviour.\n- **lz4hc.c** (rows 179–222): `LZ4MID_compress`, `hashChain`, `compress_optimal`, `LZ4HC_encodeSequence`'s two `return 1` sites, all clevel clamping, obsolete-API inverted return conventions.\n- **xxhash.c** (rows 223–235): the two `XXH_ERROR` sites, `createState` allocation, and the *missing* NULL checks.\n- **Out-of-range FFI enums** (rows 1–8, 26–31): documented per-field where the C validates vs. silently masks.\n\n## Findings worth flagging to the translation effort\n\n1. **`LZ4F_getBlockSize`'s error return is never checked by its two callers** (`lz4frame.c:389`, `:740`). An out-of-range `blockSizeID` in `LZ4F_preferences_t` becomes `maxBlockSize = (size_t)-2` and flows into `LZ4F_compressUpdate`'s block loop — a real dst-overflow hazard, not a clean error. `LZ4F_writeOpen` (`lz4file.c:246`) is the *only* API that validates a caller-supplied `blockSizeID` up front.\n2. **`blockChecksumFlag == 2` produces a corrupt frame silently**: the FLG byte stores `&_1BIT` (→0) but `LZ4F_makeBlock` advances `((U32)crcFlag)*BFSize` = 8 bytes (`:789` vs `:903-907`).\n3. **`LZ4F_compressUpdateImpl:1013-1017` lacks `FORWARD_IF_ERROR`** on its internal `LZ4F_flush` — an error code is added to `dstPtr` as if it were a byte count.\n4. **`LZ4F_writeClose` swallows earlier write failures** (`lz4file.c:325-340`): if `errCode` was latched, `compressEnd` is skipped and `LZ4F_OK_NoError` is returned, leaving an unterminated frame.\n5. **Two genuinely dead error sites**: `lz4file.c:162` (`io_read`, unreachable — `size_t` can't be negative) and `lz4file.c:124` (`maxBlockSize_invalid` on a decoded 3-bit field already validated by `decodeHeader`).\n6. **`LZ4_setStreamDecode` can never return 0** despite its documented `0 == error` contract (`lz4.c:2589-2602`).\n7. **`XXH32_reset`/`XXH64_reset` do not NULL-check `statePtr`** — they `memcpy` into it. The task brief anticipated `XXH_ERROR` here; the actual code has no such check, so a Rust port must not model this as a recoverable error.\n8. **`*_continue` decoders conflate empty output with failure** (`result <= 0` → early return, state un-advanced) at `lz4.c:2640/2653/2662/2685/2694/2703`.\n\nThe closing note lists the unreachable `LZ4F_ERROR_*` codes with reasons: `GENERIC`, `blockMode_invalid`, `compressionLevel_invalid`, `srcSize_tooLarge` (never emitted at all), `allocation_failed` (environmental only), `maxCode` (sentinel), plus the conditionally-compiled-out checksum/magic errors under `FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION`.","usage":{"total_tokens":192866,"tool_uses":36,"duration_ms":456526},"uuid":"1678158b-707e-470d-8e6b-64777ef0a1d2","session_id":"fbbc4e99-c89f-4b88-83bb-165c018df800"}
