{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_g5i4puqwvseimieost744dbmtv4vmd25dpap6c6hb6rbypuzbbtq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-gKqcQz/translation/CONFIGS.md` written: **145 rows**, numbered sequentially 1..145, 196 lines, 10 `## ` sections exactly as specified (xxhash, lz4 block one-shot, lz4 block streaming, lz4hc, lz4hc streaming, deprecated/legacy API, lz4frame one-shot, lz4frame streaming, lz4frame dictionary, lz4file). Block-decompression one-shot rows live in \"lz4 block one-shot\" and streaming-decode rows in \"lz4 block streaming\" to keep to the requested subheading set. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified.\n\nAxes derived from source, with the concrete constants that drive the branching:\n\n- **xxhash** (`src/xxhash.c`): `XXH32_finalize` switches on `len&15` → 6 distinct paths (case 0; 1/2/3; 4/8/12; 5/9/13; 6/10/14; 7/11/15), each crossed with the `len>=16` accumulator. `XXH64_finalize` switches on `len&31` → 10 paths, crossed with `len>=32`. Streaming adds `memsize+len<16` (resp. 32) buffer-only, `memsize!=0` merge, bulk loop, leftover copy, and the `large_len` flag being settable either from a single big chunk *or* from accumulated `total_len_32>=16`, which changes the `digest` branch.\n- **lz4 block** (`src/lz4.c`): `LZ4_64Klimit` = 64KB+MFLIMIT−1 = 65545 selects `byU16` vs `byU32`; `LZ4_minLength` = 13; `srcSize==0` has an explicit empty-block shortcut; acceleration clamps at `<1 → 1` and `>65537 → 65537`; `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset` picks `dictSmall` vs `noDictIssue` from `ctx->currentOffset`; `LZ4_prepareTable` resets on tableType change / `inputSize>=4KB` / `currentOffset>1GB`. `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` has 6 distinguished modes: prefix+dictSmall, prefix+noDictIssue, `usingDictCtx` (input ≤4KB), dictCtx-memcpy+`usingExtDict` (input >4KB), extDict+dictSmall, extDict+noDictIssue — plus tiny-dict (<4) invalidation and src/dict overlap fixups. `*_usingDict` fan out on `dictSize==0` / contiguous-and-`>=64KB−1` / contiguous-and-smaller / separate buffer; `_safe_continue` on `prefixSize==0` / `>=64KB−1` / `<64KB−1 && extDictSize==0` / `doubleDict` / wraparound-`forceExtDict`.\n- **lz4hc** (`src/lz4hc.c`): `k_clTable` gives 3 strategies — level 1–2 `lz4mid`, 3–9 `lz4hc` hashChain (nbSearches 4…256), 10–12 `lz4opt` (96/512/16384, level 12 also enables `fullUpdate`/ultra); `<1 → 9`, `>12 → 12`. `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` is **2**, not 3 — so lz4frame's fast-vs-HC split is at level 2, and level 2 already goes down the HC context path. `isStateCompatible` (mid vs non-mid) plus `position>=64KB` and `position==0 && srcSize>4KB` select the three dictCtx paths.\n- **lz4frame** (`src/lz4frame.c`): `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` always forces `autoFlush=1`, `stableSrc=1`, runs `LZ4F_optimalBSID` (shrinks blockSizeID when srcSize is small) and forces `blockIndependent` when `srcSize <= blockSize` — so one-shot prefs are not passed through verbatim. `compressBegin` buffer sizing is a 2×2 matrix over `autoFlush` × `blockMode` (0 / 64KB / blockSize / blockSize+128KB). Decode is a 15-state machine; the distinguishing inputs are src fed in fragments (all `store*` stages), dst smaller than `maxBlockSize` (tmpOut + `flushOut` + the four `LZ4F_updateDict` modes), `stableDst`, `skipChecksums`, stored/uncompressed blocks (`copyDirect` + `getBlockChecksum`), skippable frames, and concatenated frames.\n- **lz4file** (`src/lz4file.c`): `blockSizeID` → `srcBufMaxSize`/`maxWriteSize` switch (default and max64KB both 64KB), `LZ4F_write` chunking at `maxWriteSize`, and `LZ4F_readOpen`'s fixed `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX` pre-read leaving 0–12 residual bytes depending on header length."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":188372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens"